    "comparison_to_boost": {
      "status": "DERIVED_CONDITIONAL_NOT_LEAN_PROOF",
      "argument": "Under the still-required strong-H1 derivative/inner-product transport, B0(s) acts on the same null profile by a(q,u)->a(q,exp(s)u). With H1 measure dq du/u and the real orthogonal screen matrix independent of u, derivative u*partial_u cancels 1/u. Thus HasBoostEnergy would have b=B_form(h), with no pi factor. This predicts M_raw=(2*pi)^3*b.",
